Sure! Below is a simple example of an **interactive rotating card** using only HTML and CSS.  
When you hover over the card, it rotates 180° around its Y‑axis (you can change the axis or angle if you like).

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Container that holds the card */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;            /* Center horizontally */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Allows children to be positioned in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth animation */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate the card */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide the backside when facing away */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #fff;
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
}

/* Styling for front side */
.card .front {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b); /* Warm gradient */
}

/* Styling for back side */
.card .back {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #43cea2, #185a9d); /* Cool gradient */
  transform: rotateY(180deg); /* Flip it so it's visible after rotation */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front face -->
    <div class="front">
      <span>Front Side</span>
    </div>
    <!-- Back face -->
    <div class="back">
      <span>Back Side</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Sets the *perspective* so the 3D rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | Holds both sides, uses `transform-style: preserve-3d` to keep child elements in 3D space. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Each side is absolutely positioned on top of each other. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that’s turned away from the viewer. |
| `.back` | Rotated 180° initially so that when the parent rotates, this side becomes visible. |

Feel free to replace the gradients, text, or add images inside the `<span>` tags. You can also tweak the `transition` duration or use `rotateX` / `rotateZ` for different rotation axes. Enjoy experimenting!
